{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline","id":1531251,"title":"The Mnemosyne as a Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-21T14:15:58-08:00","id":1531251,"title":"The Mnemosyne as a Bloodline","content":"I like bookish characters. In canon, the jury is still out whether or not the Mnemosyne (and their imo rather lazily conceived opposite number in the Sabbat, the Jocastians) qualify as a 'proper' bloodline, but let's assume they are.<br /> <br /> I remember reading <i>somewhere </i>their Discipline spread would be Auspex, Obfuscate, and Presence, which would work for a Malkavian bloodline. Their Flaw was fittingly an obsession with arcane secrets in the same source, but I really can't remember which one that was. Some MET thing perhaps?<br /> <br /> Anyways, I think that's fine overall, but perhaps I would extent the Flaw and focus to general mysticism instead of just Noddism.<br /> <br /> How would you outfit the Bloodline? Maybe adjust the Background to something different than a straight-up Malkavian line? Perhaps give them a signature Discipline? I read that they got one in Requiem, but I'm not sure it's particularly interesting from what I got from the wiki. Do they still appear in V5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T22:21:19-08:00","id":1531273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline#post1531251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like bookish characters. In canon, the jury is still out whether or not the Mnemosyne (and their imo rather lazily conceived opposite number in the Sabbat, the Jocastians) qualify as a 'proper' bloodline, but let's assume they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the &quot;Jocastian/Jocastatians as Sabbat&quot; angle is 100% Revised era or V20 late nonsense. Doubly so if one considers <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aristotle_de_Laurent\" target=\"_blank\">De Laurent</a>'s own dealings with the Montreal Sabbat in Revised era. Damn, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ayisha\" target=\"_blank\">Ayisha</a> got her copy of Laurent's compilation of the Book of Nod from Beckett, of all people!<br /> <br /> And what she does? Makes a huge printing run of it because, in her own words, making it available only to some princes and primogen is ridiculous unfair! That combined with her whole paragraph dissembling on her own (im)probable loyalties and motives to do such a thing in the Book of Nod's postface kind of screams hard &quot;Anarch trolling&quot;, imho.<br /> <br /> Also, technically speaking every neonate or ancilla coterie in WoD with one or two pocket-sized copies of the Book of Nod, not to mention reprints or scanlations of it, possibly owes this woman (and Beckett) a solid - for what is basically the undead Wikileaks scandal of its time. Think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline#post1531251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading <i>somewhere </i>their Discipline spread would be Auspex, Obfuscate, and Presence, which would work for a Malkavian bloodline. Their Flaw was fittingly an obsession with arcane secrets in the same source, but I really can't remember which one that was. Some MET thing perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Auspex, Obfuscate, and Presence is cited by De Laurent himself in the many notes to his edition of the Book of Nod, ditto for the obsession, if memory tricks me not.<br /> If MET puts that in a gameplay ready package or adds anything else for that matter honestly i wouldn't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline#post1531251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I think that's fine overall, but perhaps I would extent the Flaw and focus to general mysticism instead of just Noddism.<br /> <br /> How would you outfit the Bloodline? Maybe adjust the Background to something different than a straight-up Malkavian line? Perhaps give them a signature Discipline? I read that they got one in Requiem, but I'm not sure it's particularly interesting from what I got from the wiki. Do they still appear in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they get a Requiem version and no, the wiki article does it nowhere near anything like justice. If you want the Mnemosyne to be more generally occult-obsessed than mono-focused into kindred origins i would <b>really </b>advise looking for them in the Mekhet clanbook - truth be told, the book in its entirety should be of good use to you, since &quot;<i>going progressively weirder and crazier the more they learn and capable at detecting all kinds of secret patterns they become</i> is very much&quot; is very much a schtick of the Mekhet as a whole, i dare say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-22-2024, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T11:31:51-08:00","id":1531299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531273#post1531273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the &quot;Jocastian/Jocastatians as Sabbat&quot; angle is 100% Revised era or V20 late nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>My head-canon for the relationship between Jocastians and Mnemosyne is that they are the same Bloodline and the controversy between them is just a big show to justify their presence in either sect and gain access to their resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531273#post1531273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Auspex, Obfuscate, and Presence is cited by De Laurent himself in the many notes to his edition of the Book of Nod, ditto for the obsession, if memory tricks me not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, thanks for that. I think I haven't looked into the Book of Nod for decades and completely dismissed it as a possible source.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531273#post1531273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they get a Requiem version and no, the wiki article does it nowhere near anything like justice. If you want the Mnemosyne to be more generally occult-obsessed than mono-focused into kindred origins i would <b>really </b>advise looking for them in the Mekhet clanbook - truth be told, the book in its entirety should be of good use to you, since &quot;<i>going progressively weirder and crazier the more they learn and capable at detecting all kinds of secret patterns they become</i> is very much&quot; is very much a schtick of the Mekhet as a whole, i dare say.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will have a look. I ignored Requiem when it came out and never caught up, but it looks like it explored plenty of interesting ideas that didn't get a spotlight in Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T21:31:15-08:00","id":1531338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531299#post1531299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head-canon for the relationship between Jocastians and Mnemosyne is that they are the same Bloodline and the controversy between them is just a big show to justify their presence in either sect and gain access to their resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how Ayisha and Beckett conspired - supposedly - behind De Laurent's back to get his edition of the Book of Nod printed &amp; distributed at large, i'd say it's perfectly possible. Truth be told i have to Dread Names as long a real long read to get a better grasp of V20's take on Ayisha, not to mention the &quot;OG Anathema&quot; that still figure in the list.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531299#post1531299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, thanks for that. I think I haven't looked into the Book of Nod for decades and completely dismissed it as a possible source.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering how the whole book is 100% fluff, it's easy to miss something like Aristotle commenting IC on his lineage's disciplines or people who helped him learn some others.<br /> (Or notes where he comments on the translation a fragment - and how some of them were decidedly less biblical-sounding than the &quot;liberties&quot; he took in translating them to a format his patrons would approve, might imply <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531251-the-mnemosyne-as-a-bloodline?p=1531299#post1531299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will have a look. I ignored Requiem when it came out and never caught up, but it looks like it explored plenty of interesting ideas that didn't get a spotlight in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have fun - i expected nothing when i first looked into it many years ago and yet my 1st/2nd ed-loving tired heart got hooked big time for more than a decade. It's a thing its own but definitely worth the look for reference and inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-23-2024, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T01:52:14-08:00","id":1531340,"title":"","content":"From the Book of Nod preface:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristotle de Laurent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barely a night goes by that I do not thank our Founder for his foresight in providing me with the secret ways of hiding, the way to see beyond sight, and the voice of command [...]</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristotle de Laurent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Tremere friend has written me, saying that the burning need [for knowledge] driving my bloodline might be the cause of the Madness. It must be true, for I cannot fight the burning desire for more knowledge, it is as difficult to resist as the need for sleep or the need for blood.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure this is the source I was thinking of, but upon re-reading it, he's clearly talking about Clan Malkavian rather than the Mnemosyne, and Dominate rather than Presence. I think the latter suits them much better though, maybe that is why I had misremembered it that way. But taken on their own, these quotes would indicate that the Mnemosyne are more of a lower-case bloodline than a capital B Bloodline. Not that it matters for what-ifs, but that was actually surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T14:41:10-08:00","id":1531386,"title":"","content":"Spinning a bit to make it click better...<br /> <br /> The Mnemosyne could be a Children of Osiris type of deal where the 'bloodline' is more defined through a common philosophy and accompanying signature Discipline. If they are rooted within the Malkavians, that Discipline could be a variation of Dementation - expressed in the acquisition of knowledge - that carries the thirst for it as a required or consequential Derangement. Hm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}